 "notes": [
  "IMG_5417 and IMG_5416 carry a street musician (sustained notes in A and D major, A = 437-439 Hz, +20-30 dB over the noise in 16k-point spectra). Under the organ score and through the kitchen glass that would be a second, unrelated music, so every city bed is detoned: sustained tonal lines are pulled down to the noise floor around them (tonal prominence 20.9 -> 11.9 dB, the noise baseline; footsteps, voices' breath and the air are kept).",
  "The kitchen clips' tracks have mains hum (50/100/150 Hz, +17-36 dB) and appliance lines (100, 161, 179, 223, 299, 401 Hz); the mains line sits at 49.3 Hz in these clips. Notched at 49.3, 50, 100-250, 223 and 300 Hz and detoned from 40 Hz: every line is now within 4 dB of its neighbours. IMG_5421's handling knock (src 4.02-5.02) and a tick at src 19.93-20.33 are replaced by clean material of the same clip. IMG_5422's own track is not used.",
  "Speed: the clips' own sound follows the cue sheet's speed curve (0.8x, 0.5x, eased ramps) through rubberband, pitch kept; library textures under the slow motion are laid on the same curve (rate 1.25: real speed where the picture is at 0.8x, 0.625x in the 0.5x stretch). Nothing is slowed by resampling; only the drips and the kettle's set-down are pitched (by resampling, to make them smaller or heavier) and they are not time-locked to frames. Rubberband processes the two channels together (apart, it decorrelated the water: L/R 0.95 -> 0.42) and uses its short window (less smear; pre-echo on a click 8-10 ms at 0.625-0.8x, about 14 ms at 0.5x). The steady first stream is not stretched at all.",
  "Set-downs: the metal kettle on its base is Mixkit 2934 pitched down 2 semitones (a dull contact; the brief had 3148), set down left, where the spout leaves frame (IMG_5421 src 0-17). The glass server's set-down (3148) is left out: under the score's build it stayed masked even 8 dB up, and it is not a story beat. The cup on the stone sill is 2933, at the cue sheet's cup_on_sill (the score's brass is off just before it; +2.5 dB).",
  "turn_away -> sill: the catalogue has no cloth rustle; nothing is added (the street runs on, continuous).",
  "The score is placed at 0 if its file exists at mix time; its gain is set so that the city stem sits 6.5 dB under it at the climax (window climax-0.5 .. climax+2.5); it is faded out from end+0.25 to end+1.35 so that the city is the last sound. It is ducked 6 dB for 1.5 s from its return after the latch (the city's first moment at full range is heard; the organ grows out of it). Its own accents are held on its bus at -4 dBFS after the master (release 0.3 s), so the master limiter does not duck the city with them.",
  "The score is ridden 2 dB down in the kitchen (music_keys; the step is in its silence after the latch): with the 23:36 score the kitchen music sat 4-7 dB higher against the water and the kettle than before.",
  "Before the latch the city behind the glass is not heard under the score's forte (about 18 LU under it): it is texture in the kitchen's quiet moments, not a voice pressing on the pane.",
  "Fader ride (mix_keys): the quiet kitchen (walk, bloom, brew, the hush) +6 dB, back to 0 over the first 2 s of the pour (the score's build to the latch is left as composed); the climax -1.5 dB: the loudness range fits a phone speaker (LRA 18 -> 13 LU) and the climax is still the loudest moment. Limiter release 200 ms (40 ms pumped under organ pedal)."
 ],
